  m_Name: 1819 indian
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: 'Indian Traders and Laborers 1819 '
  info: Following the establishment of Singapore as a British trading post, Indian
    merchants arrived to participate in commerce. Tamils, Gujaratis, and Sindhis
    established thriving businesses, while laborers worked on infrastructure projects.
    Temples like Sri Mariamman Temple were built, serving as religious and cultural
    hubs for the growing Indian community.
